{"meta": {"title": "Vahiny Mianatra Malagasy — Starter Content Pack", "description": "Core vocabulary and phrases for a beginner English speaker (elderly learner). Sources: Peace Corps Malagasy Language Lessons (public domain) and bako.blog lessons.", "version": "1.0", "audience": "Elderly American beginner learner"}, "pronunciation": {"vowels": [{"letter": "a", "sound": "like 'a' in FATHER", "examples": ["salama (hello)", "manana (to have)"]}, {"letter": "e", "sound": "like 'ay' in MADE, PAY", "examples": ["veloma (bye)", "teny (word)", "enina (six)"]}, {"letter": "i / final y", "sound": "like 'ee' in KEEP, LEEK", "examples": ["misy (there is)", "tsia (no)"]}, {"letter": "o", "sound": "like 'oo' in POOL, SUE", "examples": ["aho (I)", "voky (full)"]}, {"letter": "ts", "sound": "like 'ts' in ITS", "examples": ["tsotra (simple)"]}, {"letter": "tr", "sound": "'tr' pressed hard (like TRAIN, tenser)", "examples": ["tratra (chest)"]}, {"letter": "dr", "sound": "'dr' pressed hard (like DRIVE, tenser)", "examples": ["drafitra (draft)"]}, {"letter": "j", "sound": "like 'dz' (as in BRIDGE), NOT like English 'j'", "examples": ["zaza (baby)", "onja (wave)"]}, {"letter": "ao", "sound": "two-vowel glide 'ah-oo'", "examples": ["vaovao (new)"]}, {"letter": "oa", "sound": "glide 'oh-ah'", "examples": ["soa (good)"]}, {"letter": "ndr", "sound": "n + hard dr", "examples": ["indrindra (especially)"]}], "notes": ["There is no verb 'to be' — pronouns alone carry it: 'aho' means both 'I' and 'I am'.", "No grammatical gender, no verb conjugation by person: mihinana (eat) → nihinana (ate) → hihinana (will eat); only the first letter changes.", "The Malagasy alphabet has no c, q, u, w, x.", "Malagasy sentence order is Verb + Object + Subject: 'Mihinana vary aho' literally = 'Eats rice I' = I eat rice.", "Stress is usually on the next-to-last syllable."]}, "phrase_units": [{"id": "greetings", "title": "Greeting People & Saying Goodbye", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_2.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Manao ahoana?", "en": "Hello! (official/central)", "note": "Pronounced ah-oo-nah"}, {"mg": "Salama!", "en": "Hi! (works everywhere)", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Salama tompoko!", "en": "Hello, sir/madam! (respectful)", "note": "'Tompoko' is the respectful address for any adult"}, {"mg": "Inona no vaovao?", "en": "What's new?", "note": "Typical follow-up greeting"}, {"mg": "Tsy misy!", "en": "Nothing special! (standard reply)", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Manakory ianao?", "en": "How are you? (Tsimihety/Bako form)", "note": "'Manao ahoana?' also used"}, {"mg": "Tsara fa misaotra.", "en": "I'm fine, thank you.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tonga soa!", "en": "Welcome! (to someone arriving)", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Veloma!", "en": "Bye!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mandrapihaona!", "en": "See you later!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Misaotra!", "en": "Thank you!", "note": "The most important word of all"}, {"mg": "Misaotra betsaka!", "en": "Thank you very much!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Azafady!", "en": "Please / excuse me / sorry", "note": "All-purpose courtesy word"}, {"mg": "Miala tsiny!", "en": "Sorry / excuse me", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tsy misy olana!", "en": "No problem!", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "introductions", "title": "Introducing Yourself", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_3.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Iza no anaranao?", "en": "What is your name?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Ruth no anarako.", "en": "My name is Ruth. (official: name first + 'no anarako')", "note": "Tsimihety: 'Anarako Ruth'"}, {"mg": "Faly mahafantatra anao!", "en": "Happy to meet you!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Avy aiza ianao?", "en": "Where are you from?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Avy any Etazonia aho.", "en": "I am from the United States.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Inona ny asanao?", "en": "What do you do (for a living)?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mianatra teny malagasy aho.", "en": "I am learning Malagasy.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Manambady aho.", "en": "I am married.", "note": "'Tsy manambady aho' = I am not married"}, {"mg": "Manana zanaka aho.", "en": "I have children.", "note": "'Tsy manana zanaka aho' = I have no children"}, {"mg": "Mipetraka aiza ianao?", "en": "Where do you live/stay?", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "polite_expressions", "title": "Polite Expressions", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_8.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Eny", "en": "Yes", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tsia", "en": "No", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Azafady …", "en": "Please… (give me …, please)", "note": "Add what you need after it"}, {"mg": "Misaotra indrindra!", "en": "Thank you so very much!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tsy misy olana.", "en": "You're welcome / no problem", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mazotoa!", "en": "Keep it up! (encouragement when parting or working)", "note": "Very Malagasy"}, {"mg": "Soa anie.", "en": "Good luck / may it go well.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Ampy izay!", "en": "That's enough!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Azo?", "en": "Understand? / OK?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Azo!", "en": "Understood! / OK!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Avia aty!", "en": "Come here!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Andraso!", "en": "Wait!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Ndao handeha!", "en": "Let's go! / Come on!", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "basic_needs", "title": "Basic Needs & Feelings", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_6.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Reraka aho.", "en": "I am tired.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Noana aho.", "en": "I am hungry.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Voky aho.", "en": "I am full (from eating).", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mangetaheta aho.", "en": "I am thirsty.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mafana aho.", "en": "I am hot.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mangatsiaka aho.", "en": "I am cold.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Aiza ny kabone?", "en": "Where is the toilet?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Te hisotro rano aho.", "en": "I want to drink water.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Te hatory aho.", "en": "I want to sleep.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Te hisakafo aho.", "en": "I want to eat a meal.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Te hivoaka aho.", "en": "I want to go out.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Marary aho.", "en": "I am sick.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Vonjeo!", "en": "Help!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mila dokotera aho.", "en": "I need a doctor.", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "small_talk", "title": "Small Talk & Reactions", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_12.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Mahafaly ahy izany.", "en": "That makes me happy.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mampalahelo izany.", "en": "That's sad.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mahagaga izany.", "en": "That's surprising!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mahasosotra izany.", "en": "That's shocking!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mandrеraka izany.", "en": "It's tiring.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mampihomehy izany.", "en": "That's funny / hilarious!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tsara ny toetrandro.", "en": "The weather is nice.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mafana androany.", "en": "It's hot today.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mangatsiaka androany.", "en": "It's cold today.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Avy ny orana.", "en": "It's raining. (The rain has come)", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "market", "title": "At the Market — Shopping", "peace_corps_audio": "MG_Malagasy_Lesson_9.mp3", "items": [{"mg": "Ohatrinona ity?", "en": "How much is this?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Ohatrinona ny …?", "en": "How much is the …?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Lafo be!", "en": "That's too expensive!", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mora ve?", "en": "Is it cheap?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Mila … aho azafady.", "en": "I need …, please.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Omeo … aho azafady.", "en": "Give me …, please.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Afaka mahazo … ve aho azafady?", "en": "May I have a …, please?", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Tsy ampy ny volako.", "en": "I don't have enough money.", "note": ""}, {"mg": "Ity ny volanao.", "en": "Here is your change. (lit. your money)", "note": ""}]}], "vocabulary_groups": [{"id": "family", "title": "Family", "items": [{"mg": "fianakaviana", "en": "family"}, {"mg": "dada / ray", "en": "father"}, {"mg": "neny / reny", "en": "mother"}, {"mg": "dadabe", "en": "grandfather"}, {"mg": "nenibe", "en": "grandmother"}, {"mg": "zanaka", "en": "child (one's own child)"}, {"mg": "zaza", "en": "child, baby (general)"}, {"mg": "zoky", "en": "older sibling"}, {"mg": "zandry", "en": "younger sibling"}, {"mg": "vady", "en": "spouse"}, {"mg": "manam-bady", "en": "married"}, {"mg": "namana", "en": "friend"}, {"mg": "anadahy", "en": "younger brother (of a woman)"}, {"mg": "anabavy", "en": "younger sister (of a man)"}, {"mg": "rahalahy", "en": "brother (of a man)"}, {"mg": "raha-vavy", "en": "sister (of a woman)"}]}, {"id": "food", "title": "Food & Drink", "items": [{"mg": "sakafo", "en": "food / a meal"}, {"mg": "vary", "en": "rice"}, {"mg": "laoka", "en": "side dish eaten with rice"}, {"mg": "mofo", "en": "bread"}, {"mg": "hena", "en": "meat"}, {"mg": "henakisoa", "en": "pork"}, {"mg": "henomby", "en": "beef"}, {"mg": "akoho", "en": "chicken"}, {"mg": "trondro", "en": "fish"}, {"mg": "atody", "en": "egg"}, {"mg": "legioma", "en": "vegetables"}, {"mg": "anana", "en": "greens"}, {"mg": "voankazo", "en": "fruit"}, {"mg": "voatabia", "en": "tomato"}, {"mg": "akondro", "en": "banana"}, {"mg": "mananasy", "en": "pineapple"}, {"mg": "manga", "en": "mango"}, {"mg": "voasary", "en": "orange"}, {"mg": "papay", "en": "papaya"}, {"mg": "ovy", "en": "potato"}, {"mg": "mangahazo", "en": "cassava"}, {"mg": "katsaka", "en": "corn"}, {"mg": "vomanga", "en": "sweet potato"}, {"mg": "rano", "en": "water"}, {"mg": "dite", "en": "tea"}, {"mg": "kafe", "en": "coffee"}, {"mg": "ronono", "en": "milk"}, {"mg": "siramamy", "en": "sugar"}, {"mg": "sira", "en": "salt"}, {"mg": "sakay", "en": "chili pepper"}, {"mg": "menaka", "en": "oil"}, {"mg": "episy", "en": "spices"}]}, {"id": "numbers", "title": "Numbers", "items": [{"mg": "iray", "en": "one"}, {"mg": "roa", "en": "two"}, {"mg": "telo", "en": "three"}, {"mg": "efatra", "en": "four"}, {"mg": "dimy", "en": "five"}, {"mg": "enina", "en": "six"}, {"mg": "fito", "en": "seven"}, {"mg": "valo", "en": "eight"}, {"mg": "sivy", "en": "nine"}, {"mg": "folo", "en": "ten"}, {"mg": "roapolo", "en": "twenty"}, {"mg": "efapolo", "en": "forty"}, {"mg": "zato", "en": "hundred"}, {"mg": "arivo", "en": "thousand"}, {"mg": "alina", "en": "ten thousand"}, {"mg": "hetsy", "en": "hundred thousand"}, {"mg": "vola / ariary", "en": "money / Malagasy currency"}, {"mg": "Ohatrinona? / Ohatrinona ity?", "en": "How much (is this)?", "note": "Compound numbers are read right-to-left: 21 = 'iraika ambin'ny roapolo' (one-and-twenty)"}]}, {"id": "colors", "title": "Colours", "items": [{"mg": "manga", "en": "blue"}, {"mg": "manga tanora", "en": "light blue"}, {"mg": "manga antitra", "en": "dark blue"}, {"mg": "mena", "en": "red"}, {"mg": "fotsy", "en": "white"}, {"mg": "mainty", "en": "black"}, {"mg": "maintso", "en": "green"}, {"mg": "mavo", "en": "yellow"}, {"mg": "mavokely", "en": "pink"}, {"mg": "volam-boasary", "en": "orange"}, {"mg": "volon-tsokolà", "en": "brown"}, {"mg": "volon-davenona", "en": "grey"}]}, {"id": "days_and_time", "title": "Days & Time Words", "items": [{"mg": "Alatsinainy", "en": "Monday"}, {"mg": "Talata", "en": "Tuesday"}, {"mg": "Alarobia", "en": "Wednesday"}, {"mg": "Alakamisy", "en": "Thursday"}, {"mg": "Zoma", "en": "Friday"}, {"mg": "Sabotsy", "en": "Saturday"}, {"mg": "Alahady", "en": "Sunday"}, {"mg": "omaly", "en": "yesterday"}, {"mg": "androany", "en": "today"}, {"mg": "rahampitso", "en": "tomorrow"}, {"mg": "maraina", "en": "morning"}, {"mg": "atoandro", "en": "noon"}, {"mg": "tolakandro", "en": "afternoon"}, {"mg": "hariva", "en": "evening"}, {"mg": "alina", "en": "night"}]}, {"id": "question_words", "title": "Question Words", "items": [{"mg": "iza?", "en": "who?"}, {"mg": "aiza?", "en": "where?"}, {"mg": "inona?", "en": "what?"}, {"mg": "firy?", "en": "how many?"}, {"mg": "amin'ny firy?", "en": "at what time?"}, {"mg": "oviana?", "en": "when?"}, {"mg": "ohatrinona?", "en": "how much?"}, {"mg": "fa maninona?", "en": "why?"}, {"mg": "ahoana?", "en": "how?"}, {"mg": "ve?", "en": "(yes/no question marker)", "note": "Placed at the end: 'Amerikana ve ianao?'"}, {"mg": "angaha?", "en": "(doubt question marker)", "note": ""}]}, {"id": "pronouns", "title": "Personal Pronouns", "items": [{"mg": "aho", "en": "I"}, {"mg": "ianao", "en": "you (one person)"}, {"mg": "izy", "en": "he / she"}, {"mg": "isika", "en": "we (inclusive — includes the listener)"}, {"mg": "izahay", "en": "we (exclusive — not you)"}, {"mg": "ianareo", "en": "you (plural)"}, {"mg": "izireo", "en": "they"}]}]}